===Austrian People's Party (ÖVP)===
Justice Minister [[Wolfgang Brandstetter]] declined to stand on 26 December 2015.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.news.at/a/brandstetter-bundespraesident-wahl-keine-kandidatur |title=Brandstetter tritt nicht an • |website=News.at |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> On 7 January 2016, ÖVP leader [[Reinhold Mitterlehner]] announced that [[Erwin Pröll]], the ''[[Landeshauptmann]]'' of Lower Austria, would not be running.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://derstandard.at/2000028654762/Erwin-Proell-tritt-nicht-zur-Praesidentenwahl-2016-an |title=Pröll: "Man muss wissen, wo man hingehört" – Bundespräsident – derStandard.at › Inland |website=Derstandard.at |date=8 January 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> [[Josef Pühringer]], ''Landeshauptmann'' of Upper Austria declined to stand on 8 January 2016,{{citation needed|date=July 2016}}<!-- WP:RS needed; removed link to WP:SPS (Twitter, FB, WP)--> as did former European Commissioner [[Franz Fischler]] and Member of the European Parliament [[Othmar Karas]]. President of the Austrian Federal Economic Chamber [[Christoph Leitl]] only said he would not comment before the announcement by the party leadership on 10 January 2016.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://diepresse.com/home/politik/innenpolitik/4900219/Wer-wird-OVPKandidat-Wurde-nicht-angerufen |title=Wer wird ÖVP-Kandidat? "Wurde nicht angerufen" " |publisher=Diepresse.com |date=30 October 2015 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> Controversial former chancellor [[Wolfgang Schüssel]] was briefly considered as a candidate, but he also declined.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://kurier.at/politik/inland/hofburg-wahl-auch-schuessel-wurde-als-oevp-kandidat-angefragt/175.257.568 |title=Hofburg-Wahl: Auch Schüssel wurde als ÖVP-Kandidat angefragt |website=Kurier.At |date=16 January 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> Other names mentioned were former Science Minister and university professor {{Interlanguage link multi|Karlheinz Töchterle|de}}, former Foreign Minister [[Ursula Plassnik]] and former Raiffeisen Zentralbank manager {{Interlanguage link multi|Christian Konrad|de}}.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://derstandard.at/2000028672230/Die-moeglichen-Kandidaten-fuer-die-Praesidentenwahl |title=Präsidentenwahl: Berichte über Kandidatur von Khol – ÖVP – derStandard.at › Inland |website=Derstandard.at |date=8 January 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://orf.at/stories/2317888/2317889/ |title=Spekulationen über Kandidatur von Khol – news.ORF.at |website=Orf.at |date=8 January 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|author1=Rainer Nowak|author2=Thomas Prior|author3=Hedi Schneid |url=http://diepresse.com/home/politik/innenpolitik/4900484/Hofburg_Khol-als-Plan-B-nach-ProllAbsage |title=Hofburg: Khol als Plan B nach Pröll-Absage « |date=9 January 2016 |publisher=Diepresse.com |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> On 10 January 2016, former first president of the National Council [[Andreas Khol]] was announced as the ÖVP's candidate.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://derstandard.at/2000028780586/OeVP-Kandidat-Khol-als-Ansage-in-Richtung-FPOe-Waehler |title=Khol ist ÖVP-Kandidat – Bundespräsident – derStandard.at › Inland |website=Derstandard.at |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref>

