===Freedom Party of Austria (FPÖ)===
[[Norbert Hofer]], who serves as the [[List of presidents of the National Council of Austria|Third President of the National Council]], had been considered the most likely [[Freedom Party of Austria]] (FPÖ) candidate. On 28 December 2015 he said that he considered himself too young for the office and that he would prefer his party to pick someone else as its candidate.<ref>[https://neuwal.com/2015/12/28/norbert-hofer-im-zib2-gespraech-zum-jahreswechsel-transkript/ Norbert Hofer (FPÖ) im #zib2 Gespräch zum Jahreswechsel #transkript] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160126141537/https://neuwal.com/2015/12/28/norbert-hofer-im-zib2-gespraech-zum-jahreswechsel-transkript/ |date=26 January 2016 }} Neuwal, 28 December 2015.</ref> Other possible candidates included President of the Austrian Court of Audit Josef Moser, former Mayor of Vienna's 1st district [[Ursula Stenzel]],<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.kleinezeitung.at/s/politik/innenpolitik/4901018/FPOEntscheidung-fur-HofburgKandidaten-noch-vollig-offen |title=FPÖ-Entscheidung für Hofburg-Kandidaten noch "völlig offen" > Kleine Zeitung |website=Kleinezeitung.at |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> ombudsman Peter Fichtenbauer<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.nachrichten.at/nachrichten/politik/innenpolitik/Der-lange-Schatten-der-Hofburg-Wahl;art385,1938622 |title=Der lange Schatten der Hofburg-Wahl |website=Nachrichten.at |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> and possibly party leader [[Heinz-Christian Strache]] himself.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://mobil.derstandard.at/2000028792104/Schwarze-fuerchten-sich-vor-dem-blauen-Mann |title=Gerüchte über Strache-Kandidatur bei Präsidentenwahl – Bundespräsident – derStandard.at › Inland |website=Mobil.derstandard.at |date=4 March 2000 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> As of 11 January 2016, Fichtenbauer, Moser and Stenzel continued to be the most likely candidates.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://derstandard.at/2000028837158/Hofer-Strache-als-blauer-Hofburg-Kandidat-unwahrscheinlich |title=Hofer: Strache als blauer Hofburg-Kandidat "unwahrscheinlich" – Bundespräsident – derStandard.at › Inland |website=Derstandard.at |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> Strache announced on 13 January 2016 that he would not be running himself, and that it was still open whether the FPÖ would nominate anyone at all.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.nachrichten.at/nachrichten/politik/innenpolitik/Strache-will-nicht-Bundespraesident-werden;art385,2084039 |title=Strache will nicht Bundespräsident werden |website=Nachrichten.at |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> In mid-January, Vienna Vice-Mayor Johann Gudenus and former FPÖ leader and former Vice-Chancellor [[Norbert Steger]] were also mentioned as possible candidates.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.oe24.at/oesterreich/politik/Gudenus-und-Stenzel-als-FPOe-Favoriten/220275335 |title=Gudenus und Stenzel als FPÖ-Favoriten |website=Oe24.at |date=17 January 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> On 19 January 2016, author and Middle East/migration pundit [[Karin Kneissl]] was mentioned as being recruited by the FPÖ to run,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.heute.at/news/politik/art23660,1251207 |title="Anfrage von der FPÖ": Hofburg-Wahl: Nahost-Expertin Kneissl lehnt Angebot ab |website=Heute.at |access-date=5 April 2016 }}{{Dead link|date=September 2026 |bot=InternetArchiveBot }}</ref> which she quickly declined.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.kkneissl.com/de |title=AKTUELLES – Deutsch |language=de|publisher=Kkneissl.com |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref>

On 20 January 2016, media reported that Gudenus had been internally selected as the FPÖ's candidate;<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.oe24.at/oesterreich/politik/Hofburg-FPOe-setzt-voll-auf-Gudenus/220701618 |title=Hofburg: FPÖ setzt voll auf Gudenus |website=Oe24.at |date=20 January 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> on 26 January 2016, reports claimed Stenzel would be announced on 28 January 2016 as the FPÖ's candidate.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.trend.at/politik/stenzel-fpoe-kandidatin-bundespraesidentenwahl-6206905 |title=Stenzel als FPÖ-Kandidatin für Bundespräsidentenwahl praktisch fix |website=Trend.at |date=26 January 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016 |archive-date=30 March 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160330183920/http://www.trend.at/politik/stenzel-fpoe-kandidatin-bundespraesidentenwahl-6206905 |url-status=dead }}</ref> Amid strong FPÖ-internal dissent, there were rumours the party leadership had been forced to reconsider, and that Hofer was now the most likely option, after all,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://kurier.at/politik/inland/nun-schlittert-auch-fpoe-in-hofburg-chaos-stenzel-durch-shitstorm-verhindert/177.512.736 |title=Basis-Aufstand gegen Straches Hofburg-Kandidatin Stenzel |website=Kurier.At |date=27 January 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> with Gudenus also still in play.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.tt.com/politik/11050726-91/blauer-spannungsbogen-entlang-der-hofburg-wahl.csp |title=Blauer Spannungsbogen entlang der Hofburg-Wahl &#124; Tiroler Tageszeitung Online – Nachrichten von jetzt! |publisher=Tt.com |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> Commentators opined that the backtracking was a notable defeat for Strache.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://kurier.at/politik/inland/strache-verliert-schon-die-vorwahl-fuer-die-hofburg/177.644.586 |title=Strache verliert schon die Vorwahl für die Hofburg |website=Kurier.At |date=28 January 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|author=Von Ulrike Weiser |author2=Thomas Prior |url=http://diepresse.com/home/politik/innenpolitik/4913437/Praesidentenwahl-treibt-tiefen-Keil-in-die-FPO |title=Präsidentenwahl treibt tiefen Keil in die FPÖ |date=28 January 2016 |publisher=Diepresse.com |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> Hofer was announced as the FPÖ's candidate on 28 January 2016.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://derstandard.at/2000029915296/FPOe-praesentiert-um-11-Uhr-ihren-Hofburgkandidaten |title=Kein Fairnessabkommen mit Norbert Hofer – Bundespräsident – derStandard.at › Inland |website=Derstandard.at |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref>

