===Alexander Van der Bellen (Independent)===
In early January 2016, it was announced that former [[The Greens – The Green Alternative|Greens]] party leader and former [[Social Democratic Party of Austria|Social Democratic]] party member [[Alexander Van der Bellen]] would run as an independent candidate.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://orf.at/stories/2317681/ |title=Bundespräsident: Van der Bellen nicht grüner Parteikandidat – news.ORF.at |website=Orf.at |date=7 January 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> Van der Bellen announced his candidacy on 8 January 2016.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://diepresse.com/home/politik/innenpolitik/4900153/Van-der-Bellen-tritt-bei-BundespraesidentenWahl-an- |title=Bundespräsidenten-Wahl: Van der Bellen tritt an « |date=8 January 2016 |publisher=Diepresse.com |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> Van der Bellen suspended his party membership of [[The Greens – The Green Alternative|Greens]] before the election to demonstrate his independence. In spite of this, the [[The Greens – The Green Alternative|Greens]] continued to be a leading supporter of Van der Bellen's campaign.

The [[NEOS – The New Austria and Liberal Forum]] leader Strolz stated that they would consider giving him the same support as Griss, depending on the same kind of hearing she went through.<ref>{{cite web|author=Iris Bonavida |url=http://diepresse.com/home/politik/innenpolitik/4900716/Neos_Grosse-Sympathien-fur-Van-der-Bellen |title=Neos: "Große Sympathien" für Van der Bellen « |date=8 January 2016 |publisher=Diepresse.com |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref>

