===Other candidates===
Independent candidate [[Irmgard Griss]], a former [[Supreme Court of Justice (Austria)|Supreme Court of Justice]] judge and its president, declared her candidacy on 17 December 2015. She presented her candidacy to the [[Freedom Party of Austria]] and [[NEOS – The New Austria|NEOS]], but both declined to endorse her.<ref>[http://derstandard.at/2000027683882/Erste-Grossspende-fuer-Griss-Praesidentschaftskampagne 100.000 Euro: Erste Großspende für Griss' Kampagne] Der Standard, 18 December 2015 {{in lang|de}}</ref> NEOS said they would support Griss and any other independent candidates indirectly, and voiced their concerns over the strong partisan politicization of the presidential office and the election campaign.<ref>[http://www.vienna.at/neos-begruessen-griss-kandidatur-zur-bundespraesidentin-ausserordentlich/4555134 NEOS begrüßen Griss Kandidatur zur Bundespräsidentin “außerordentlich”] Vienna Online, 18 December 2015</ref> NEOS leader [[Matthias Strolz]] stated on 9 February 2016 that NEOS might also support Van der Bellen, voicing his preference for a run-off election between Griss and Van der Bellen.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.nachrichten.at/nachrichten/politik/innenpolitik/Neos-wollen-Griss-und-Van-der-Bellen-unterstuetzen;art385,2118162 |title=Neos wollen Griss und Van der Bellen unterstützen |website=Nachrichten.at |date=2 January 2015 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref>

