[[Richard Lugner]], society figure, businessman and candidate for president in [[1998 Austrian presidential election|1998]], was reported to be considering running again,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://orf.at/stories/2316164/2316163/ |title=Politjahr im Zeichen der Hofburg-Wahl – news.ORF.at |website=Orf.at |date=2 January 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> and stated on 8 February 2016 that he would very likely be running.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.ots.at/presseaussendung/OTS_20160208_OTS0163/lugner-in-oesterreich-trete-vermutlich-an |title=Lugner in ÖSTERREICH: "Trete vermutlich an" &#124; Mediengruppe "Österreich" GmbH, 08.02.2016 |language=de|website=Ots.at |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> He announced his candidacy on 10 February 2016, citing a poll carried out for him by the Humaninstitut which showed him on 10% (behind Van der Bellen on 27%, Hundstorfer on 18%, Hofer on 17%, Griss at 15% and Khol on 13%).<ref>{{cite web|url=http://diepresse.com/home/politik/innenpolitik/4922748/ |title=Hofburg-Wahl: Lugner tritt an « |date=10 February 2016 |publisher=Diepresse.com |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref>

