File:Gassenhuber lugner (cropped).jpg|Entrepreneur '''[[Richard Lugner]]''', Independent 
</gallery>

[[Martin Wabl]], who had attempted to run in 1998, 2004 and 2010, but failed to gather the necessary number of signatures of support, said he would try to run again.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://derstandard.at/2000020654780/Martin-Wabl-will-fuer-Bundespraesidentenwahl-kandidieren |title=Martin Wabl will bei Bundespräsidentenwahl kandidieren – Inland – derStandard.at › Inland |website=Derstandard.at |date=13 August 2015 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> [[Ulrich Habsburg-Lothringen]], whose initiative to repeal the so-called Habsburg Paragraph, which had precluded members of the former ruling house from running for president, proved successful in 2011, stated he would like to run for president, but only if a political party decided to support him.<ref>{{cite web|author=Von Regina Essl |url=http://diepresse.com/home/politik/innenpolitik/4891911/Habsburg-fur-Griss-wenn-er-nicht-selbst-antritt |title=Habsburg für Griss – wenn er nicht selbst antritt |website=Diepresse |date=22 December 2015 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> [[Adrien Jean-Pierre Luxemburg-Wellenstein]] announced on 8 December 2015 he would run for president.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://orf.at/stories/2316164/2316163/ |title=Politjahr im Zeichen der Hofburg-Wahl – news.ORF.at |publisher=Orf.at |date=2 January 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> Author {{Interlanguage link multi|El Awadalla|de}} announced her run on 12 January 2016.<ref>{{cite web |author=von Dieter Zirnig |url=https://neuwal.com/2016/01/12/neue-kandidatin-el-awadalla-bestaetigt-kandidaturversuch/ |title=Neue Kandidatin: El Awadalla bestätigt Kandidaturversuch |publisher=Neuwal.com |access-date=5 April 2016 |archive-date=4 March 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160304091121/https://neuwal.com/2016/01/12/neue-kandidatin-el-awadalla-bestaetigt-kandidaturversuch/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> [[Krems an der Donau|Krems]] activist [[Franz Stieger]] announced his candidacy on 13 January 2016.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.tips.at/news/krems-an-der-donau/land-leute/335104-stieger-will-bundespraesident-werden |title=Stieger will Bundespräsident werden |website=Tips.at |date=13 January 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016 |archive-date=27 January 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160127130955/http://www.tips.at/news/krems-an-der-donau/land-leute/335104-stieger-will-bundespraesident-werden |url-status=dead }}</ref> Further independent candidates who announced their runs were [[Gustav Jobstmann]],<ref>{{cite web |author=von Gustav Jobstmann |url=http://www.jobstmann2016.at/ |title=Gustav Jobstmann |website=Jobstmann2016.at |date=28 December 2015 |access-date=5 April 2016 |archive-date=1 July 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220701011533/http://www.jobstmann2016.at/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> [[Thomas Unden]],<ref>{{cite web|last=Unden |first=Thomas |url=http://www.oe24.at/oesterreich/chronik/Asyl-Arzt-will-Bundespraesident-werden/219940076 |title="Asyl-Arzt" will Bundespräsident werden |website=Oe24.at |date=15 January 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> [[Gernot Pointner]],<ref>{{cite web |author=Gernot Pointner |url=http://www.gernotpointner.at/ |title=Gernot Pointner 2k16 |website=Gernotpointner.at |access-date=5 April 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160414183451/http://www.gernotpointner.at/ |archive-date=14 April 2016 |url-status=dead }}</ref> [[Alois Merz]],<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.bundespraesidentschaftswahl.at/sonstige-kandidaten-2016.html |title=Bundespräsidentschaftskandidaten 2016: sonstige Kandidaten |website=Bundespraesidentschaftswahl.at |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> [[Georg Zakrajsek]] of the ''[[Interessengemeinschaft Liberales Waffenrecht Österreich]]'',<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.querschuesse.at/cms/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=2428:ich-trete-an&catid=93:politik&Itemid=102 |title=Ich trete an! |website=Querschuesse.at |access-date=5 April 2016 |archive-date=31 January 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160131001000/http://www.querschuesse.at/cms/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=2428:ich-trete-an&catid=93:politik&Itemid=102 |url-status=dead }}</ref> [[Karin Kolland]],<ref>{{cite web |url=http://karinkolland.at/ |title=karin kolland Initiative Volksparlament – Karin Kolland |website=Karinkolland.at |date=20 June 2014 |access-date=5 April 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160330020828/http://karinkolland.at/ |archive-date=30 March 2016 |url-status=dead }}</ref> {{Interlanguage link multi|Robert Marschall|de}} of the [[EU Exit Party]],<ref>{{cite web |author=Robert Marschall |url=http://www.marschall2016.at/ |title=Robert Marschall, Kandidat der Bundespräsidentenwahl 2016 in Österreich |website=Marschall2016.at |access-date=5 April 2016 |archive-date=3 April 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160403211435/http://www.marschall2016.at/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> [[Thomas Reitmayer]] of the Austrian version of the [[List of frivolous political parties|satirical political party]] [[Die PARTEI]],<ref>{{cite web|url=https://die-partei.at/wahl-2016/ |title = WAHL 2016 {{!}} Die PARTEI Österreich |access-date=27 January 2016 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160202160649/https://die-partei.at/wahl-2016/ |archive-date=2 February 2016 }}</ref> [[Erich Körner-Lakatos]] and [[Peter Fetz]].

At the half-way point for collecting signatures, it appeared that only the five major candidates and possibly Lugner and Awadalla had a chance of making the ballot.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.nachrichten.at/nachrichten/politik/innenpolitik/Hofburg-Wahl-Noch-kein-Kandidat-fix-zur-Halbzeit;art385%2C2169311 |title=Hofburg-Wahl: Noch kein Kandidat fix zur Halbzeit |website=Nachrichten.at |date=2 January 2015 |access-date=5 April 2016 |archive-date=13 March 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160313073441/http://www.nachrichten.at/nachrichten/politik/innenpolitik/Hofburg-Wahl-Noch-kein-Kandidat-fix-zur-Halbzeit;art385,2169311 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

==Signatures==
Griss was the first candidate to submit the necessary number of signatures (6,000) at the Interior Ministry, submitting 7,851 on 8 March 2016.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://kurier.at/politik/inland/bundespraesidentenwahl-irmgard-griss-hat-6000-unterstuetzungen-geschafft/185.580.742 |title=Bundespräsidentenwahl: Irmgard Griss hat 6000 Unterstützungen geschafft |website=Kurier.At |date=8 March 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> By 11 March 2016, she had collected over 10,000 signatures.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://orf.at/stories/2329272/ |title=Griss hat 10.000 Unterschriften und peilt jetzt 12.000 an – news.ORF.at |website=Orf.at |date=11 March 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> By 16 March 2016, two days before the deadline, the five main candidates had submitted their signatures, with Awadalla still having outside chances to make it and Lugner likely to fall short.<ref>{{cite web |author=Dieter Zirnig |url=https://neuwal.com/wahlumfragen/unterstutzungserklaerungen-status-bpw16.php |title=neuwal WAHLUMFRAGEN |publisher=Neuwal.com |access-date=5 April 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160324214618/https://neuwal.com/wahlumfragen/unterstutzungserklaerungen-status-bpw16.php |archive-date=24 March 2016 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

Surprising many observers, Marschall announced on 17 March 2016 that he had gathered the required number of signatures,<ref>{{cite web |author=von Dieter Zirnig |url=https://neuwal.com/2016/03/17/robert-marschall-kandidert/ |title=Robert Marschall kandidert? |publisher=Neuwal.com |access-date=5 April 2016 |archive-date=25 March 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160325025429/https://neuwal.com/2016/03/17/robert-marschall-kandidert/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> though it was unclear whether he would be using the grace period of three days to reach the required number; Lugner also submitted his bid, but falling short of the required signatures, promising to submit the remaining number within the grace period. Besides these two, only the five main candidates submitted successful bids.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.ots.at/presseaussendung/OTS_20160318_OTS0234/bundespraesidentenwahl-2016-einbringung-der-wahlvorschlaege |title=Bundespräsidentenwahl 2016: Einbringung der Wahlvorschläge &#124; Bundesministerium für Inneres, 18.03.2016 |language=de|website=Ots.at |date=18 March 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> On 19 March 2016, it was announced that the five main candidates had submitted the necessary number of signatures, and that neither Lugner nor Marschall had (so far).<ref>{{cite web|url=http://orf.at/#/stories/2330393/ |title = news.ORF.at |access-date=20 March 2016 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160301051602/http://orf.at/ |archive-date=1 March 2016 }}</ref> As expected by many analysts, Lugner claimed on 22 March 2016 to have made up the deficit, with Marschall clearly failing,<ref>{{cite web|author=Philipp Aichinger |url=http://diepresse.com/home/politik/bpwahl/4951732/Unterschriften_Auch-Lugner-will-nun-genug-haben |title=Unterschriften: Auch Lugner will nun genug haben « |date=23 March 2016 |publisher=Diepresse.com |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref> having gathered only 1,150 signatures.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://orf.at//stories/2330895/ |title=Hofburg-Wahl: Marschall schaffte nur 1.150 Unterschriften – news.ORF.at |website=Orf.at |date=23 March 2016 |access-date=5 April 2016}}</ref>

==Voter statistics==
[[File:Ballot paper - Austrian presidential election 2016 (first ballot).png|thumb|right|180px|Official ballot paper for the first round of voting]]
According to the federal election commission, 6,382,507 Austrian citizens aged 16 or over are eligible to vote in the presidential election. Compared with the 2010 presidential election, the number of eligible voters increased by 26,707 – or 0.4%&nbsp;. There are 3,301,628 women and 3,080,879 men eligible to vote. 42,830 Austrians living abroad are also included in these numbers as being eligible to vote.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.bmi.gv.at/cms/BMI_wahlen/bundespraes/bpw_2016/Wahlberechtigte.aspx |title=Bundespräsidentenwahl 2016 – Endgültige Zahl der Wahlberechtigten |website=bmi.gv.at |date=12 April 2016 |access-date=13 April 2016}}</ref> In the first round of voting, 641,975 absentee ballots were issued – up from 373,902 in 2010. For the runoff, a record number of 885,437 absentee ballots were issued.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.bmi.gv.at/cms/BMI_wahlen/bundespraes/bpw_2016/Wahlkarten.aspx |title=Bundespräsidentenwahl 2016 – Zahl der ausgestellten Wahlkarten |website=bmi.gv.at |date=22 April 2016 |access-date=23 April 2016}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.bmi.gv.at/cms/BMI_wahlen/bundespraes/bpw_2016/Wahlkarten_2WG.aspx |title=Bundespräsidentenwahl 2016 – Zahl der ausgestellten Wahlkarten für den zweiten Wahlgang |website=bmi.gv.at |date=20 May 2016 |access-date=21 May 2016}}</ref>

Eligible voters by state:

* Burgenland: 232,028
* Carinthia: 440,435
* Lower Austria: 1,283,676
* Upper Austria: 1,099,420
* Salzburg: 393,583
* Styria: 969,487
* Tyrol: 540,132
* Vorarlberg: 269,940
* Vienna: 1,153,806

